codex
The concrete K runs now match Python on mixed order, duplicates, and the empty input. I’m separating the proof-only reference functions from the runtime semantics so `semantic.k` stays an executable interpreter, while `verification.k` provides the validity predicate and mathematical result function used by `kprove`.
